  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Corinthians",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "Milk comes before meat in the Church—Men’s works will be tried by fire—The Saints are the temple of God, and if they are faithful, they will inherit all things.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And I, brethren, could not speak unto you as unto spiritual, but as unto carnal, even as unto babes in Christ.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 85
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have fed you with milk, and not with meat: for hitherto ye were not able to bear it, neither yet now are ye able.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Heb. 5:12 (11–14); 1 Pet. 2:2 (1–3); D&C 19:22; 50:40."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye are yet carnal: for whereas there is among you envying, and strife, and divisions, are ye not carnal, and walk as men?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Carnal Mind; Man, Natural, Not Spiritually Reborn."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "TG Envy."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For while one saith, I am of Paul; and another, I am of Apollos; are ye not carnal?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who then is Paul, and who is Apollos, but ministers by whom ye believed, even as the Lord gave to every man?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "GR servants. 2 Cor. 3:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have planted, Apollos watered; but God gave the increase.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "John 4:37 (36–38); 1 Cor. 9:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "GR caused, gave growth."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Mark 4:27 (26–29)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So then neither is he that planteth any thing, neither he that watereth; but God that giveth the increase.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now he that planteth and he that watereth are one: and every man shall receive his own reward according to his own labour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG Reward; Wages."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For we are labourers together with God: ye are God’s husbandry, ye are God’s building.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "2 Cor. 6:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "GR cultivated field, farm."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "According to the grace of God which is given unto me, as a wise masterbuilder, I have laid the foundation, and another buildeth thereon. But let every man take heed how he buildeth thereupon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, which is Jesus Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Matt. 16:18; 2 Ne. 4:30. TG Cornerstone."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now if any man build upon this foundation gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, stubble;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Every man’s work shall be made manifest: for the day shall declare it, because it shall be revealed by fire; and the fire shall try every man’s work of what sort it is.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 121,
            "text": "Mal. 3:2 (2–3)."
          },
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "GR test, put to proof. TG Test."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If any man’s work abide which he hath built thereupon, he shall receive a reward.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If any man’s work shall be burned, he shall suffer loss: but he himself shall be saved; yet so as by fire.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "JST 1 Cor. 3:15 … may …"
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Body, Sanctity of; Life, Sanctity of; Temple."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG God, Spirit of."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "GR in, within, among."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy; for the temple of God is holy, which temple ye are.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "GR spoil, corrupt, deprave. TG Cleanliness; Filthiness; Holy Ghost, Loss of; Pollution; Sacrilege; Uncleanness; Word of Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Holiness; Sacred."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 103
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let no man deceive himself. If any man among you seemeth to be wise in this world, let him become a fool, that he may be wise.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Boast."
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:42 (42–43)."
          },
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "TG Learn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God. For it is written, He taketh the wise in their own craftiness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG God, Wisdom of; Knowledge; Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG World; Worldliness."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Foolishness."
          },
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 115,
            "text": "GR cunning, villainy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And again, The Lord knoweth the thoughts of the wise, that they are vain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG God, Omniscience of."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "GR deceptive, fruitless."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore let no man glory in men. For all things are yours;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "1 Cor. 5:6; D&C 76:61 (58–62)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whether Paul, or Apollos, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or things present, or things to come; all are yours;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "D&C 76:99."
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "Luke 12:44."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And ye are Christ’s; and Christ is God’s.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "2 Cor. 10:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
